{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal by reasons of the height, bulk, plot width and design of the proposed dwelling, would be a dominant and incongruous feature that is cramped on site which would fail to provide a coherent pattern of development in the street scene thus would substantially harm the form, and proportion of the site and streetscene. This would be detrimental to the pattern of development within the surrounding area and would therefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the Adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The application fails to provide sufficient and accurate information to demonstrate how the proposed development would achieve the statutory minimum 10% Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG), as required by the Environment Act 2021. In the absence of this information, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the development would not result in a net loss of biodiversity or that it would deliver the required net gain. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies G6 of the London Plan (2021), CS1 of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and DM20 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal would result in an additional residential dwelling being sited on garden land. As such, the principle of the development is contrary to the Harrow Core Strategy of directing new residential and other development to the Harrow and Wealdstone Opportunity Area, town centres and, in suburban areas, to strategic previously developed sites and would therefore harm its implementation, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies CS1.A and CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Garden Land Development (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
